{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/180849-help-with-ciphers-and-interlocks","id":180849,"title":"Help with Ciphers and Interlocks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T09:24:42-07:00","id":180849,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Help with Ciphers and Interlocks","content":"If your Demon Name is Arta Fabrash or Mr. Horn or your cover name is Benjamin Wallace, please do not read this thread.<br /> <br /> So, I need some help making Ciphers for my Demons. I've got some ideas but I'm quite stumped for interlocks. Unfortunately, since we've already played quite a few sessions one Demon is a single question away from his 2nd Key and another has already got his 2nd Key. I told him I needed some time to write out the Interlock for him. To do that I need to actually have that interlocks, so here goes.<br /> <br /> First is Mr. Horn, aka Harold Lowe, a reporter with The Stranger, an alternative weekly newspaper in Seattle. Technically he's on the Arts staff and does music reviews, but he also fills in with whatever sort of text they need that week. His function in this Cover before he fell was to make sure that The Stranger always went to print a certain number of characters long. The Demon is an Inquisitor Messenger, and he is very much people focused. His 1st Key was &quot;Find the Leak&quot;, and I have given him the 2nd Key of &quot;Trust No One&quot;. The idea was to make an Interlock such that it make people who talked to him unlikely to confess.<br /> <br /> My second Demon is Arta Fabrash, aka Tim Travers, a Security Consultant and Private Investigator. He was the personal bodyguard of a Mr. d'Argentan before he Fell, but he murdered this man shortly after his Fall. His Tim Travers cover is currently the Seattle PD's lead suspect in that murder case, though a key witness has recanted seeing him at the scene of the crime before it happened(thanks to Mr. Horns Memory Editing Process). Arta Fabrash is a Saboteur Guardian, with a very sort of gung-ho go out and do it attitude. Where Mr. Horn is about People, Arta Fabrash is about Action. His 1st Key is &quot;Authorized&quot;, and he does not yet have his 2nd Key of &quot;Never Here&quot;, though he knows its an embed he doesn't have, uses Manipulation, and is Mundane. The idea here was that the people would not report his investigations.<br /> <br /> As you can see, my ideas for the first two interlocks are very similar. I'd like that not to be the case, and I still have time to switch the 2nd Key of Arta Fabrash to &quot;Alibi&quot;, &quot;Diversion&quot;, &quot;Don't I know you?&quot;, &quot;Earworm&quot;, &quot;Homogenous Memory&quot;, &quot;Identity Theft&quot;, &quot;Idle Conversation&quot;, &quot;Interference&quot;, &quot;Living Recorder&quot;, &quot;Meaningless&quot;, &quot;Occam's Razor&quot;, &quot;Quick Change&quot;, &quot;Unperson&quot;, &quot;Without a Trace&quot; from the main text or &quot;Associate and Integrate&quot;, &quot;Deep Cover&quot;, &quot;Mistaken Identity&quot;, &quot;The Voting Dead&quot;, or &quot;You can tell me&quot; from Flowers of Hell. Ideally I'd move to Cacophony or Instrumental embeds for the 3rd and 4th Keys for Arta Fabrash, to reinforce his penchant for decisive action.<br /> <br /> There is a third Demon, Benjamin Wallace, but he's not yet joined our game or finished making a character. So I don't yet know is 1st Key. I suspect it might be Fungible Knowledge or Living Recorder. From what the player has given me so far that character with be about Information. He's not a computer hacker like many other players seem to me making, but he does have a technical skill set. I have an idea for his Final Truth if he is in fact about Information, the phrase &quot;It from Bit&quot; by John Wheeler a famous physicist about the concept of Digital Physics, that information not stuff is the building blocks of the Universe.<br /> <br /> The final piece of context is the game that I am running. It does take place in Seattle, though so far I haven't really had the players run into any of the stuff from the Demon book. The opponent is a Cult of the God Machine called The Splinter in the Eye, though they don't know that name yet. Physically the cult is centered about the University of Washington in the city. Metaphysically it is about removing the Splinters of Time in the City of Seattle that dog the God Machine's plans. It has quite a lot of power in Seattle, particularly in several University Departments. It's leader and patron is a United States Congressman, with an Angel as his Personal Assistant.<br /> <br /> The cult has two projects, one of which the players have found. The one they've found is the Temporal Pins, which is trying to keep the Splinters from getting bigger or any worse. They do this by recruiting the homeless with promise of a better life, and use them to kill people simultaneously in the Prime timeline and the Splinters. These people must never have left the City of Seattle in their lives. This was how the two original Demons Fell, they were assigned to kill a man named John Harrison in two of the Splinters while a hobo killed him in the prime timeline. They both refused this order and Fell. Following the trail of Mr. Harrison's murder in the Prime Timeline has lead them to the recruiting apparatus and making inroads on the Cult.<br /> <br /> The project they don't know about is creation of Infrastructure, specifically an Atomic Clock with an Occult Matrix which will reconcile the Splinter Timelines with the Prime and eliminate them. It's being made by an engineering professor at UoW, but he's not a cultist. Instead he's having his dreams manipulated by them using a family heirloom, a clock with human bone gears. They break often, and are continually replaced by the bones of the dead killed by the Mayor and Sherriff of a small town outside Seattle who made a deal to keep their town from dying. There are more parts, but that's the premise.<br /> <br /> The idea is that this will lead to a final internal conflict with the Demons. The God Machine Cult is doing Evil, killing people and manipulating them. But it is also doing Good, in the prevention of degradation of the timeline of Seattle and they eventually will also completely cure the city of it's Temporal problem. This is something I really want to relate to Arta Fabrash's Final Truth, because there is a question of whether destroying the Atomic Clock is actually a good idea. And who would it be good for? Humanity? Demons? The God Machine?<br /> <br /> But that leaves the question, how do I get Arta Fabrash form his 1st Key of &quot;Authorized&quot; to a final truth about action vs. inaction? And where should Mr. Horn's Cipher lead him? I just don't know that. Any suggestions? And thanks for reading my admittedly longwinded explanation of my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3378-leonfoucault","user":"LeonFoucault","date":".  Paragraph Spacing 06-26-2014, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3378-leonfoucault","name":"LeonFoucault","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}